# SBOB-EXAMPLES DEMO WATERMARK — synthetic auditd corpus, scenario A (M3).
#
# Sustained-repetition corpus: 8 rounds of the drift families (an environ
# sweep read, a credential-file read, the exfil connect) within 120s in ONE
# wazuh-logtest session. Expected on the 8th round:
#   100222  sustained open drift   (8 undeclared opens in 120s)
#   100232  sustained connect drift (8 undeclared peers in 120s)
# Honest label: the REAL stealer connects exactly ONCE (single-POST semantics,
# no retry), so 100232 is a capability proof on synthetic repetition, not an
# incident replay; 100222 is realistic the other way (60-80 credential files
# under the collector cap). 100212 (sustained exec) and 100209 (sustained
# sensitive) are asserted ABSENT: no exec drift and no watchlist path in this
# scenario (see drift.audit honest absences).
